Section D records the accuracy posture for the Section Nine Speed and right of way dossier. Every knowledge fact is required to trace to its cited physical handbook page, with the cited page stating the fact. Confidence is high across the section because every rule comes from the single pinned handbook edition, and every number is spelled out in words so that the card backs read aloud exactly. The extracted text of these pages carries a font-encoding shift that turns commas into line breaks and interleaves the hand-signal figure captions; the dossier author decoded the shift deterministically and matched each hand-signal label to its caption by their printed order. Although the section id names right of way, the two pages mapped to it cover speed, slow driving and signaling; the right-of-way rules themselves appear on the lane use and passing pages and are carried in that section's dossier. Handbook wording is paraphrased throughout; no official sentence, table, image or question is reproduced. Designated speed limits are stated as the pinned edition prints them; no time-variable fact beyond that edition appears, so nothing required isolation as dynamic knowledge.
